age":"D1: anchor R1's loader, its test and its one run outside v1\n\nIn v1's run, R1 raised ValueError before the engine ran: anchors._load\nhanded B2's sparse matrix to SimpleData, which takes only a dense array\n(core.py:122). The dry runs' backgrounds are dense, so no run took this\npath. DEVIATIONS.md D1 records the change before any run:\n- anchors._load cuts a sparse file to the panel's N_GENES genes by the\n  panel's rule (the named genes, then the most expressed) and makes it\n  dense; r1 names Xist and the Y genes;\n- a dense file (B3) is unchanged;\n- the metric, the claims and the allowed outcomes are unchanged;\n- src/ stays the tag's (its tree and sha256 are recorded).\n\ntest_anchors.py takes the sparse path on synthetic files only. On the tag's\nanchors.py it fails at core.py:122.\n\nanchors-r1.yml runs R1 once, after the results and outside v1. It starts on\nthe label \"r1-run\". The run commit is the tag plus D1's three files, and\nthe result goes as it is to results/panel-v1-r1. v1's results stay as\npublished.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MDGJh7hAAALAdwQFLhcwpp","timestamp":"2026-10-10T07:14:48Z","author":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"},"committer":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"}},"repository":{"id":1289335561,"node_id":"R_kgDOTNmzCQ","name":"metric-autopsy","full_name":"mool32/metric-autopsy","private":false,"owner":{"login":"mool32","id":200848776,"node_id":"U_kgDOC_i1iA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200848776?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mool32","html_url":"https://github.com/mool32","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mool32/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mool32/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mool32/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mool32/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_ur